-# Claude Design Field Guide
+# Claude Design Field Guide — review candidate
 
-Most AI design examples begin with a blank canvas. Product teams usually begin somewhere harder: a shipped screen, an established design system, real interaction rules, and developers who need a clear path from design intent to production code.
+Use the guide to extend an existing product screen from its design-system sources and prepare an engineering handoff. This October 2 candidate includes the refreshed guidance, a tested local Data Pipeline Studio exercise, and matching Daytime and Late night PDFs.
 
-This field guide gives product teams a way to ground a prototype in real components, extend a bounded screen, and give developers the decisions and evidence they need. Official documentation supports the workflow capabilities; the teaching example still needs hands-on testing.
+[Read the Daytime version](./output/pdf/claude-design-v1.0.0-2026-10-02-daytime-r1.pdf) · [Read the Late night version](./output/pdf/claude-design-v1.0.0-2026-10-02-late-night-r1.pdf) · [Read the manuscript](./Claude_Design_Field_Guide_Source.md)
 
